<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Mataram (Lombok)</h1><p class="st-meta">1740 CE – 1894 CE (approx.) · capital Mataram (Cakranegara)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Balinese Hindu kingdom that ruled the Muslim Sasak people of Lombok until the bloody Dutch intervention of 1894.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Princes from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-karangasem">Kingdom of Karangasem</a> had established Balinese rule in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a> by the late 17th century, displacing Makassarese influence. Several rival Balinese courts emerged on the island, and around 1740 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram</a> became the leading one; in 1838 to 1839 it defeated its rivals, uniting Lombok under a single Balinese dynasty based at Mataram and Cakranegara.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> Balinese elite ruled a majority of Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasak-people">Sasak</a> farmers, taxing their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and controlling their aristocrats. The kingdom grew rich exporting rice and became powerful enough to rule <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-karangasem">Karangasem</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> after 1849. Its Balinese princes built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pura-meru">Pura Meru</a> temple and the Mayura water palace in Cakranegara.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasak-people">Sasak</a> nobles rebelled and appealed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, who sent an expedition in 1894. After a surprise night attack destroyed part of the Dutch force, reinforcements stormed Cakranegara, where members of the royal house died in a puputan; the aged raja surrendered and died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok-treasure">Lombok Treasure</a> was taken to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, and the island joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1740 CE – 1894 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.33%;width:3.06%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1740 CE – 1894 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mataram (Cakranegara)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anak Agung Gede Ngurah Karangasem</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Balinese Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Balinese, Sasak</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lombok Kingdom, Balinese Kingdom of Lombok, Cakranegara</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1817&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mataram-lombok" aria-label="Kingdom of Mataram (Lombok) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7888 2498 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Mataram (Lombok) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8208 2754L8195 2749M8208 2754L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8195 2749h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8208 2754h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8208 2754h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mataram. <a href="/atlas?year=1817&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mataram-lombok">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
